    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented idempotent owner creation as a single new, self-contained AOP aspect \u2014 matching the repository's established pattern where every cross-cutting concern on `POST /api/owners` is an advice around `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`, leaving the controller untouched.\n\n**New file:** `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/advice/OwnerIdempotencyAdvice.java`\n\nHow it works:\n- An `@Around` advice at `@Order(Ordered.HIGHEST_PRECEDENCE)`, so it wraps every other owner-create advice (duplicate checks, quotas, response enrichers).\n- Reads the `Idempotency-Key` request header via `RequestContextHolder`.\n- No key \u2192 proceeds normally (existing behaviour unchanged).\n- First time a key is seen \u2192 proceeds, then remembers the fully-derived response (enriched by the inner `@AfterReturning` advices, since those run inside `proceed()`).\n- A repeat of a seen key \u2192 short-circuits before any duplicate check runs and returns the original owner with `200 OK` (instead of the `409` a duplicate payload would otherwise produce).\n\n**Structural impact:** zero existing functions changed; one file touched containing one small aspect (one method with CC ~3, `WMC_other` = 0). This keeps the cost near the theoretical minimum \u2014 no growth of the large controller class or any existing advice.\n\nThe full test suite (including the new `AcceptanceTest.coreIdempotentRepeat`) is green.",
