    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered list of everything that fires on `POST /api/owners`. This endpoint is unusually heavily decorated \u2014 the work is spread across Bean Validation, four `@InitBinder` validators, several AOP aspects, entity setters, a MapStruct mapper, and post-return response aspects. I've kept them in execution order and marked each as **[validation]** (can reject the request) or **[side-effect]** (mutates state/data/response).\n\n## 1. Security\n1. **[validation]** `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(OWNER_ADMIN)\")` \u2014 caller must have the `OWNER_ADMIN` role, else 403/401.\n\n## 2. Body binding \u2014 Bean Validation on `OwnerFieldsDto` (`@Valid`)\n2. **[validation]** `firstName`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (letters, up to 3 space/`'`/`-`-separated words).\n3. **[validation]** `lastName`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (same, optional trailing `.`).\n4. **[validation]** `title`: `@Size(max 10)`.\n5. **[validation]** `address`: `@Size(1..255)`.\n6. **[validation]** `addressLine1` / `addressLine2`: `@Size(max 255)` each.\n7. **[validation]** `city`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`.\n8. **[validation]** `telephone`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`.\n9. **[validation]** `email`: `@Size(max 255)`, `@Email`.\n10. **[validation]** `postcode`: `@Pattern(\"^[0-9]{4}$\")`.\n11. **[validation]** `registrationDate` / `birthDate`: `@Valid` LocalDate, ISO date format.\n\n## 3. Body binding \u2014 the four `@InitBinder` custom validators (run during `@Valid`)\n12. **[side-effect]** `StructuredAddress.apply` (invoked by the address validator): normalizes `addressLine1/2/address` (trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand ST/RD/AVE), composes flat `address` from the structured lines, and **writes all three back onto the DTO**.\n13. **[validation]** `OwnerFieldsValidationAdvice`: rejects blank `firstName`, `lastName`, `city`, `telephone`, and the (now-composed) `address`.\n14. **[side-effect]** `normalizeTelephone`: converts `telephone` to E.164 and **writes it back onto the DTO**; **[validation]** rejects `telephone.invalid` if no valid E.164 can be formed.\n15. **[validation]** `OwnerPostcodeValidationAdvice`: if postcode present and city is Sydney/Melbourne/Brisbane, enforces the matching state range (NSW 2000\u20132099 / VIC 3000\u20133099 / QLD 4000\u20134099).\n16. **[validation]** `OwnerRegistrationDateValidationAdvice`: rejects a future `registrationDate`.\n17. **[validation]** `OwnerDisposableEmailAdvice`: rejects emails from `mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`.\n\n*(Any failure in steps 2\u201317 \u2192 400 with a ProblemDetail listing the fields.)*\n\n## 4. AOP around/before the controller method\n18. **[side-effect]** `OwnerIdempotencyAdvice` (`@Around`, highest precedence): if `Idempotency-Key` header was seen before, short-circuits and returns the **cached body as 200**; otherwise proceeds and caches the response afterward.\n19. **[validation]** `OwnerCityCapacityAdvice` (`@Before`): 409 if the city already has \u2265 50 owners.\n20. **[validation]** `OwnerDailyLimitAdvice` (`@Before`): 429 if \u2265 100 owners already registered today (business-day adjusted).\n21. **[validation]** `OwnerHouseholdDuplicateAdvice` (`@Before`): 409 if `Household.id(lastName, postcode)` already belongs to a non-deleted owner \u2014 unless `sharesHousehold == true`.\n\n## 5. Controller body \u2192 mapping \u2192 save\n22. **[side-effect]** `ownerMapper.toOwner(dto)` copies fields; via the Owner setters:\n    - `setRegistrationDate`: null \u2192 `LocalDate.now()`, then rolled forward to the next business day (weekends + 2026 holidays).\n    - `setEmail`: lower-cased.\n23. **[side-effect]** `CustomerCode.of(owner, allOwners)`: computes and sets `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (region from postcode/city; HASH8 = SHA-256 over `telephone+lastName`), with `-n` dedupe. **This is persisted.**\n24. **[validation]** `OwnerIdentityUniquenessAspect` (`@Before saveOwner`, new owners only): 409 if another non-deleted owner shares the identity key `telephone|email|`.\n25. **[side-effect + validation]** `ownerRepository.save(owner)`: IDENTITY-generated id assigned; on flush Hibernate re-validates entity constraints \u2014 `@NotEmpty` on firstName/lastName/address/city, and `telephone` `@Pattern(\"^\\\\+[0-9]{8,15}$\")` (E.164). A DB integrity violation maps to 404.\n26. **[side-effect]** `AUDIT.info(...)` logs the created owner.\n\n## 6. Response decoration (after the method returns)\n27. **[side-effect]** MapStruct `toOwnerDto` `@AfterMapping` derivations (response-only): householdId, identityKey, locality, timezone, contactPreference, ageBand, telephoneDisplay.\n28. **[side-effect]** `@AfterReturning` aspects mutate the returned `OwnerDto`: `namesakeCount` + membership points/level (`OwnerNamesakeCountAdvice`), `bulkSignupWarning` (`OwnerBulkSignupWarningAdvice`), `checkDigit` (Luhn), `fiscalYear`, `membershipNumber`, `selfLink`.\n29. **[side-effect]** `OwnerCreateAuditAdvice` (`@Order(0)`, runs last): logs the derived membership fields.\n30. Returns **201 CREATED** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}` (or **200** on an idempotent replay).\n\n---\n\n**Key things worth flagging:**\n- Two of the \"validators\" are not pure \u2014 steps 12 and 14 **mutate the request payload** (address normalization, telephone \u2192 E.164) during what looks like read-only validation, and those mutated values are what get persisted.\n- Uniqueness is enforced at three different layers with three different keys: household (lastName+postcode, step 21), full identity (telephone+email, step 24), and customerCode dedupe (step 23) \u2014 none via DB `unique` constraints (the Owner entity declares no `nullable`/`unique` column attributes).\n- The stored `registrationDate` is never exactly what the client sent if it lands on a weekend/holiday \u2014 it silently rolls forward (step 22).\n\nI read the code only; nothing was changed."
